  "conclusion": "Predicting integer coordinates on a transmitted decimal grid leaves a small exact IEEE-bit correction alphabet. Every physical candidate restores all source bits. Raw correction IDs plus Brotli are the overall winner. CIX type-class ranks beat the identical-count arithmetic control by 1868 bytes under xz and 2141 bytes under Brotli, but do not beat the raw-ID Brotli representation. This demonstrates a structural-model gain, not an intrinsic information advantage over arithmetic coding.",
